<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The host runs with the hardened runtime and needs no exceptions or
  entitlements. Each one it might seem to need, and why it doesn't:
  - Network (com.apple.security.network.*): sandbox-only; the app is not
    sandboxed, and the private CGVirtualDisplay API rules the sandbox out.
    Local Network access is a privacy prompt (NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription).
  - Screen Recording: a privacy grant (NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription), not
    an entitlement.
  - Microphone (com.apple.security.device.audio-input): there is no Mac audio
    capture yet.
  - com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation: every bundled dylib is
    signed by the same team as the app, so library validation passes.
  - com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory: no
    code is generated at run time (FFmpeg, egui and wgpu don't).
  - Accessibility, for posting input: a privacy grant too, and input is not
    wired on the Mac yet.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
